# sameas — hub API keys for `--complete`
#
# TEMPLATE. Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not,
# so it must NEVER contain a real key.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     $EDITOR .env
#
# These keys are only needed for `resolve --complete`, which reaches external
# identity hubs to turn a name/address into a strong identifier (place_id,
# Placekey). Everything else — `ingest`, identifier lookups, and repeat name
# queries served from the local index — needs no keys and makes no network calls.
#
# ─── COST WARNING ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every uncached `--complete` bills real money. Google Place Details with
# `websiteUri`/phone is Google's **Enterprise** SKU, the priciest tier. Start
# with a handful of records, not a whole corpus, and check your billing page
# after the first run. `name_index` / `name_cardinality` cache results so a
# repeated (name, qualifiers) query costs nothing the second time.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Places API (New) — `places:searchText` + `places/{id}` details.
# Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Needs the "Places API (New)" enabled on the project.
# STRONGLY recommended: restrict the key to the Places API and set a quota cap.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Placekey API — street address -> placekey (the strongest place anchor).
# Sign up: https://www.placekey.io/
PLACEKEY_API_KEY=

# TMDb API — movie/TV crosswalk (imdb <-> tmdb <-> wikidata). Not needed for
# places/restaurants; leave blank unless you are resolving films.
# https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
TMDB_API_KEY=
